  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Hybrid Power Generation in Nitti, through Inglett &amp; Stubbs International, LLC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant funds a feasibility study (FS) for the development of an approximately 192 Megawatt (MW) hybrid power generation plant near the village of Nitti in Sierra Leone. The Study will assess how best to maximize the use of solar photovoltaic energy and provide reliable power generation. Because the Project has the potential to pair solar with natural gas power generation, the Study will analyze credible lower and zero-carbon alternatives to natural gas use in accordance with the Executive Order (EO) on Tackling the Climate Crisis at Home and Abroad (E.O. 14008). The Sierra Leone Ministry of Energy, on behalf of the Government of the Republic of Sierra Leone, is the proposed grantee. The proposed contractor is Inglett &amp; Stubbs International, Limited Liability Corporation (LLC).</narrative>
  </description>
